    "body": "Sometimes we don\u2019t need to give, To respond and constantly have to explain. Our purposes aren\u2019t always here to \u201cgive our all\u201d to others. Definitely not at our own expense. How did it become frowned upon so often or then become the open door of flooding questions when all you personally want to do is lie in silence, in your own divine solitude ? Sometimes our purposes aren\u2019t here to weed other peoples gardens. Sometimes our purpose is to be the fire \ud83d\udd25 starter ? The igniting force which burns away the weeds so the new blooms may blossom ? I\u2019m allowed to lock my castle gardens when I mend and prune my cascading gardens. Why should I invite you in ? Some things are sacred in solitude\u2026 Like healing\u2026 I am being reminded daily that I am the Keeper of my Keys. I own them. They were given to me as a spiritual birthright. Don\u2019t walk in my garden if you\u2019re here to pick the petals\u2026 These delicacies are all mine.",
