    "body": "Two hands\u2026 I have two hands, Capable and strong ! Used to hold a Lion Heart \u2665\ufe0f And keep it safely nestled in between my bosoms, day and night. There is no handover during this time. No space nor time which could be carried by another.\n\nI have two hands. Nurturing and healing. Used to feed, to place and prepare, The need, The necessity of life for another.\n\nI have two hands. Praying and releasing. Used to serve, to soothe, to protect The little body of a king calling out for my consciousness and presence.\n\nI have two hands. Two\u2026 One to hold, One to keep Two hands With no room in those moments for myself.\n\nI have two hands. On my breast and another calming a lullaby across your back. Given over Grace and grit. Mother and son.\n\nI have two hands, No longer my own. Two to be given. To be offered Palm to palm Breast to holy mouth. To keep close. To surrender into the belly of birth.\n\nI have two hands. Not vacant for my own feeding. Weaving, Carving, [private line held back in this public build] Preparing, But offered as a sacred alter, To a soul resting or fighting in between their imprints and warmth which are hardly available to serve anything else.\n\nI have two hands. At times, free to wash the sweat, the tears and mothers milk stains across my chest. Randomly energised to unpack washing and soothe my own skin. When time And space, And energy, Allows.",
