    "id": "fragment-042",
    "title": "It was never about you",
    "chapter": "The Blue Moon Archive",
    "tags": [
      "water",
      "fire",
      "memory",
      "blue-moon-archive"
    ],
    "body": "It was never about you. It was about the truths that lay in those deep waters. The ones you denied for decades, Until you were frozen. Lifeless in your muted form.\n\nBut I saw you... I heard you calling my name. Like a whisper of truth, Swirling, light-footed in the meadows of youth.\n\nYour womb... A nest, vacant from a falling. Those golden twines of swishing swirls. That sweet melody. Blushing with a deprived sight.\n\nI remember those perfectly infused horses. That cheer and my heart bursting with the vibrating ground. Erratic speech, Money and Mo\u00ebt flirting with the clouds. I sat there. Emotionless. Painted lips and well recited acceptance.\n\nWeak I thought. The lot of you.\n\nAs each delectable bubble burst on my tainted pallet, So did the gushing of life. Neatly, Poetically, Prose and poise:\n\n[private line held back in this public build]",
