    "body": "Dearest of all, when he arrives\u2026\n\nIt has taken me some time to process To unwrap Heal Mend Weave Question Explore Protect And understand It\u2019s not about being easy, it\u2019s only about the fact that I don\u2019t want war with invisible enemies. I do not want pieces of weakness and heaviness to pull at our ankles.\n\nI can climb, but only if the destination is towards my castle. I have been so focused on this for years. Without cheering, Without light, Stumbling my way through [private line held back in this public build] I am created to protect in actual fact. But I do not want to fight the demons if the unity I surrender into does not protect the crown. If the bonds that are created do not hold the forces at bay. I have felt ripped open and put on display in a room filled with hunger for far too long. Like an accessory to be added for an aesthetic appeal. A replacement on a shelf to take the space of something that filled its place but broke. It has always been my place in life. I do not want it anymore. I am protective of my heart because I fought lifetimes to find all the shattered ribbons of it, When all I\u2019ve wanted was a sacredness and high walls to keep me safe. I know what I have inside my flesh. I have seen what it draws near and with that, it requires so much protection. A secret hiding space. It requires always being on guard, observant and aware. The wolves like slipping in when the door to vulnerability is opened. Like an innocent lamb, they can smell. The more precious something is, the more desire and pull there is to it. As your soul has experienced through its decades of stripping.\n\nI am a warrior by spirit. I have roamed in the woods for centuries That\u2019s where I found you. Deep in the icy water. I saw you there amongst the lilies Submerged. Your face buried in the belly of emerald depths. I could hear your silent cry. And with that, I will give you my breath and my life and my tenderness, but this I can only give when you walk through my luscious gardens with the dead bodies behind. I am not a cemetery where the corpses lie. I am the journey when you have buried what weighs you down. As I need to leave behind and to not always raise my bow and arrow, you must use yours. There should be no guilt that you carry for doing what is necessary for yourself. Eliminate Let go Purge Break open Unfold But only give me the truths and the lantern to put my light in.\n\nI will fight beside you like no other. But I will not be bitten by any predators that are welcomed in. I will open your spiritual eyes to see all that lurks behind, but you need to trust my purpose. As I must trust yours. I will surrender into yours like a baptism A holy anointing I will allow you to fall in parts of me where no one has entered. I will reserve that space like a Throne Room of Grace. But you need to protect the key \ud83d\udd11 I am not a replacement I am something entirely different. I am not the fulfillment of a void but the magic of a new world. I want to feel that. I will not carry the weight of the broken women who latch on. This is not my consciousness. I request that you respect me and my weariness enough, to not bring other enemies to my rose fountains where I want to lay with you in private. Where I want to give and be given something that isn\u2019t freely given to the world. I will not abandon you on that journey, but the walk I take beside you must unfold into an alignment. I will support and guide and love and be, but please know my journey is not to share my crown \ud83d\udc51 or the hiding spaces I lead you to in order to unlock my heart. These spaces are sanctuaries of safety. A loop of protection. I will clothe you in my warmth, but do not leave me cold. I will pluck away the blindfolds and make you see, but do not give that to the world. We must remain or evolve I am evolving... And if we walk together, then letting go of the past is a weight we cannot carry. It is a separation we must both prepare for. Patterns and repetition are burdens, not protective armor. We\u2019ve become so accustomed to carrying, we have forgotten that none of it is ours to carry.\n\nI am trying to let go To surrender But we cannot do so if there is still war. I am eliminating As must you my darling, For you hold too much glory and grace for this to be given freely. You have too many treasures to protect Too much beauty to restore. I see all the galaxies inside you. The stars bursting with light and healing. The majestic creature and King that you are. I want to protect you, not fight you. Hold you in my deep embrace. Share a pure intimacy which no one can touch. But I cannot do so unless you are ready to fight off anything that feeds off you. Unless you are ready to break free from the shackles that have bound you.\n\nI will make you strong and stand tall I will fight besides you, Support you, Encourage and believe in you. But only if you are ready to not be pulled down anymore. I will be by your side and always look over your shoulder. I want you free and wild. But conscious and aware at the same time.\n\nI know I am fierce Intense Warrior-like But I have been at war my whole life. It is time for my stillness. As it is yours. I have crawled and found my way through decades to get here. My bones ache, My spirit thirsts for still waters.\n\nI have been a part of the world before, But no more.\n\nI am in the woods Running through the trees Leaving lanterns along the way. You will find me Like I found you. [private line held back in this public build] I will bow at your feet and clothe you in my cloak. [private line held back in this public build]\n\nFind what you seek The purity to embalm you like honey.",
