    "body": "For years I was stuck in the loom of hope. \u201cHope\u201d can be a cruel deceiver. A looping spiral \ud83c\udf00 An excuse to hold onto something your heart cannot accept. Hope for the best. Hold onto hope they say. Hope will get you through. But there comes a time where you need to look hope in the face and say, right now, you are not my friend. You are not kind to me and my dreams. You are not welcome with your flowers to cover up the corpses of reality. The blooms you capture in the hands of another. Sometimes you don\u2019t need hope, You need fact over fantasy. You need truth over poetry. Hope can be a self sabotaging alter, where you return again and again to be slaughtered. Calling, Waving, Knocking at your door to take you along. Hope is not enough to protect the sacredness of a child. Hope is not enough to be the only thing one holds onto.\n\nI choose truth. I choose life. I choose observation and preservation in the fact that hope is no longer a companion at my table.\n\nI choose powder blue eyes and the echo of offspring when they unfold in the safety of your sacrifice.\n\nI choose stability and consistency I choose laughter which does not intoxicate nor lure you off your chosen path.\n\nI choose freedom, Peace, Purpose, Protection I choose ME \ud83d\udd4a\ufe0f And maybe\u2026 Just maybe\u2026 Hope will one day again be welcome. But I am at peace, without hoping for that to be the case.",
